{"text": "Saltspring Wills & Estates Law Corporation\n204 - 1127 Fort Street, Victoria, BC V8V 3K9 · Tel 250-555-0116 · Fax 250-555-0117\n\nOur file: 24-0388/JKS — PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL — working draft, not\nyet sworn\n\nINVENTORY OF ASSETS AND LIABILITIES (to be exhibited to the\nForm P10 affidavit)\nEstate of AGNES ROSALIND THACKERAY, also known as Nessa Thackeray, late of\nSidney, British Columbia (the \"Deceased\")\n\nSupreme Court of British Columbia, Victoria Registry, No. VIC-P-24-1187. Prepared\nunder the Wills, Estates and Succession Act and Rule 25-3.\n\nThe Deceased was born on 3 June 1929 in Leeds and died at Lochside Manor on 11\nFebruary 2024, aged 94. Social insurance number 599 329 059. Her last will is\ndated 19 September 2011, with one codicil dated 4 May 2019. The executors are\nher nephew Callum J. Thackeray of Nanaimo and Fiona Gillespie, the Deceased's\nnext-door neighbour of thirty years.\n\nPart I — Real property\n 2281 Amelia Avenue, Sidney, BC V8L 2H6. PID 004-918-227. 2024 BC\nAssessment value C$1,148,000; appraised by Garry Oak Appraisals Ltd. at\n$1,205,000 as of the date of death.\n PID 017-442-906: undivided one-half interest in a recreational lot on Mayne\nIsland, held with her late brother's estate. Half interest: $212,500.\n\nPart II — Accounts and investments\n Arbutus Coast Credit Union, Sidney branch (transit 04810, institution 809):\nchequing 1004-883-21, balance $18,342.17; term deposit TD-7702915,\n$85,000.00, matures 30 Nov 2024.\n Dominion Maritime Bank, routing 00270-614, savings account 5530 118 947:\n$46,910.55.\n Shannonside Bank, Limerick, Ireland — an account left to her by her late\nhusband Desmond Thackeray (d. 1998) and never closed. IBAN IE86 AIBK 6006\n4571 1882 84, BIC SHNNIE2LXXX. Balance €9,418.03, roughly C$13,850.\n\n RRIF with Larchwood Securities Inc., account 77-QK41-9: $203,774.60. Callum\nis the designated beneficiary, so this passes outside the estate.\n TFSA with Larchwood, account 77-QK42-6: $61,208.11. No designation on file.\n\nPart III — Personal property\n 2014 Subaru Forester, VIN JF2SJADC5EH417726, BC plate KR4 82T, insured\nthrough ICBC. Black book value $9,800.\n 17-ft aluminium boat \"Sea Thrift\", hull no. QBC41877K213, and trailer: $3,500.\n Jewellery, including a sapphire ring appraised at $6,400, and her late\nhusband's RCAF service medals.\n Household contents, estimated: $4,000. Mr. Thackeray says Aunt Nessa kept\nabout four thousand dollars in cash in a biscuit tin. Not yet located.\n\nPart IV — Liabilities\n Lochside Manor, final account, invoice LM-24-02219: $7,912.40.\n Haywood & Stroud Funeral Chapel: $11,280.00, paid by Callum on his own Visa\non Feb. 20; to be reimbursed.\n Canada Revenue Agency, terminal T1 return, estimate only: $38,000.\n\nPart V — Beneficiaries\n Callum Thackeray — 50% of residue.\n Margaux Lachance, the Deceased's great-niece, of Gatineau, QC — 25% of\nresidue.\n Peninsula Seniors' Hospice Society — 25% of residue.\n St. Columba's Anglican Church, Sidney — legacy of $25,000. The Deceased was\na lifelong Anglican and sang in the choir there.\n Ms. Gillespie — the Mayne Island interest (specific gift under the codicil).\n\nNotes to file\nThe Deceased was diagnosed with vascular dementia in 2021 and moved to\nLochside that autumn. Margaux's mother, Odile Lachance, has hinted she may\nquestion capacity for the 2019 codicil. Ask Dr. Brandvold's office for the chart\nbefore we swear anything.\n\n 819-555-0138 is Odile's number; she phoned twice last week and wants a copy\nof the will.\n\nMs. Gillespie prefers email (fiona.gillespie@mailhaven.example) or her mobile,\n250 555 0171. Callum is at sea until the 28th; use cjthackeray@tidewrack.example.\n\nJasbir K. Sidhu, Barrister & Solicitor (Law Society of BC no. 512907) — JKS, March\n6, 2024", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "3 pages · 590 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["AGNES ROSALIND THACKERAY", "Callum Thackeray", "Margaux Lachance", "Odile Lachance", "Ms. Gillespie", "Jasbir K. Sidhu"], "companies": ["Saltspring Wills & Estates Law Corporation", "Garry Oak Appraisals Ltd.", "Arbutus Coast Credit Union", "Dominion Maritime Bank", "Shannonside Bank", "Larchwood Securities Inc.", "TFSA with Larchwood", "Limerick", "ICBC", "Royal Canadian Air Force", "Canada Revenue Agency", "Peninsula Seniors' Hospice Society", "St. Columba's Anglican Church", "Lochside Manor", "Funeral Chapel", "Mayne Island Society", "Mailhaven"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Victoria", "Sidney", "Nanaimo", "Mayne Island", "Limerick", "Lochside Manor", "Gatineau"], "health": ["vascular dementia"], "sensitive": ["British Columbia", "Lochside Manor", "race or ethnicity", "family"], "names": ["Agnes", "Nessa", "Callum", "Fiona", "Desmond", "Margaux", "Odile", "Jasbir", "Brandvold", "Steve"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 234.70000000298023, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 42, "text": "Saltspring Wills & Estates Law Corporation", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Saltspring Wills & Estates Law Corporation"}, {"start": 49, "end": 65, "text": "1127 Fort Street", "kind": "street", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "1127 Fort Street"}, {"start": 67, "end": 75, "text": "Victoria", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Victoria Registry"}, {"start": 77, "end": 79, "text": "BC", "kind": "region", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "BC"}, {"start": 80, "end": 87, "text": "V8V 3K9", "kind": "postal_ca", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "V8V 3K9"}, {"start": 94